# A Git origin stages a plain worktree: the directory a backend is handed holds the checked-out sources and no
# repository, so walking it never meets a file git is still creating and removing. The Command backend asserts that
# and then builds libanswer.a out of the staged sources, so the binary printing 42 proves the same directory the
# assertion inspected is the one that was checked out at the pinned tag.
> setupRepo
> run
